{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_proportion`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `y_proportion`, with deterministic relation `y_proportion[j] = y[j] / n[j]`, because the original likelihood scored the expression `to_vector(y) ./ to_vector(n)` and SafeStan requires a protected observation to be a plain top-level data identifier. The likelihood is otherwise unchanged. The three parameter priors were moved before the first model-block use of their parameters to satisfy SafeStan's prior-before-use rule.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int J;
  array[J] int n;
  vector[J] x;
  array[J] int y;
  vector[J] y_proportion;
  real r;
  real R;
  real overshot;
  real distance_tolerance;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_theta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_distance;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[J] p_angle;
  vector[J] p_distance;
  vector[J] p;

  sigma_theta ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_distance ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);

  p_angle = 2 * Phi(asin((R - r) ./ x) / sigma_theta) - 1;
  p_distance = Phi((distance_tolerance - overshot)
                   ./ ((x + overshot) * sigma_distance))
               - Phi((-overshot) ./ ((x + overshot) * sigma_distance));
  p = p_angle .* p_distance;
  y_proportion ~ normal(p,
                        sqrt(p .* (1 - p) ./ to_vector(n)
                             + sigma_y ^ 2));
}
generated quantities {
  real sigma_degrees;
  sigma_degrees = (180 / pi()) * sigma_theta;
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":2,"n":[5,6],"x":[6.116808687937838,5.250070477444627],"y":[5,5],"y_proportion":[1.0,0.8333333333333334],"r":2.3538227950041963,"R":6.21284185283342,"overshot":5.3638245974666034,"distance_tolerance":6.520044599062147}","protected_variables":["y_proportion"]}
